   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## WEB5 Texture and pattern (seamless tile)\nBackgrounds, paper and fabric grain, surface textures, repeating patterns. Two passes, one model:\n1. Klein draws a flat texture (1024 px square).\n2. The tile is wrapped by half so its edges meet in the middle, then Klein repaints that seam cross (feathered mask, denoise 0.75). The outer edges now tile **seamlessly**.\n\n- Check the **2x2 tiling preview**. If a cross still shows, raise *Seam fix* denoise to 0.85.\n- Prompt for *flat, evenly lit, top-down, no vignette, no focal object*. Strong light gradients or one big motif will not tile well.\n- Use the tile as a CSS `background-repeat` image. Keep it subtle behind text and re-check contrast.\n- Size is fixed at 1024 here (crops and masks depend on it). `generate.py --size` rescales all of them. Upscale with WEB6 for 2048 tiles (upscaling keeps it seamless).\n- Distilled model, 12 steps each pass, CFG 1 (~25 s)."
   ]
  },
